## 🔌 2. Native Win32 API P/Invoke in PowerShell

Call Win32 kernel methods directly without compiling separate C# binaries:

```powershell
$Signature = @"
[DllImport("kernel32.dll", SetLastError = true)]
public static extern bool SetProcessWorkingSetSize(IntPtr hProcess, IntPtr dwMinimumWorkingSetSize, IntPtr dwMaximumWorkingSetSize);
"@
$Kernel32 = Add-Type -MemberDefinition $Signature -Name "Kernel32Helper" -Namespace "Win32" -PassThru
$Kernel32::SetProcessWorkingSetSize([System.Diagnostics.Process]::GetCurrentProcess().Handle, -1, -1) | Out-Null
```

